---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    num: '01',
    name: 'Scope',
    body:
      "We fix the boundaries before anything else: which systems are in, which are out, what questions the report must answer, and the price. This goes into a one-page statement of work. If your situation doesn't fit a fixed scope — genuinely unfamiliar territory, unusual codebase — I'll say so and quote capped time-and-materials instead, with the cap in writing.",
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    name: 'Access',
    body:
      'You grant read-only access to repositories, documentation, and (where relevant) infrastructure dashboards, under a mutual NDA. I work from my own equipment, never push changes, and delete working copies when the engagement closes. If read-only access is genuinely impossible, we talk about alternatives before I commit to conclusions.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    name: 'Review',
    body:
      "I do the review personally — that's the product. Expect one batched set of written questions to your technical lead rather than a standing meeting. I read code and architecture the way a senior engineer joining your team would, plus the AI-specific checks most reviews skip: model and data governance, failure behaviour, cost under load, and whether AI-generated code has been verified by anyone.",
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    name: 'Report',
    body:
      'On the agreed date you receive the written report: a risk matrix across the agreed dimensions, findings in priority order with effort estimates, deal-breaker flags if any exist, and a two-page summary written for people who don\'t read code. Scope and method are stated inside the report, so anyone reading it later knows exactly what it does and doesn\'t claim.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    name: 'Debrief',
    body:
      "One hour, once you've read it. Walk through the findings, challenge anything that seems off, and agree what happens next. If you want help with remediation afterwards, that's a separate, clearly-scoped engagement — the report never depends on you buying more.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="How it works — Async Forest Advisory"
  description="How an assurance engagement runs: scope, read-only access under NDA, personal review, written report, one debrief. Fixed price agreed before anything starts."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h1>Scope first. One meeting. A report that stands on its own.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The whole process is built to need as little of your time as possible —
        and to make the conclusion trustworthy to someone who wasn't in the
        room.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--warm">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <ol class="process">
        {steps.map((s) => (
          <li class="process__step">
            <div class="process__head">
              <span class="process__num mono">{s.num}</span>
              <h2>{s.name}</h2>
            </div>
            <p>{s.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2>What the report promises — and what it doesn't</h2>
      <p>
        Every report is <strong>point-in-time</strong>: it describes the system
        as reviewed, on the dates stated, within the scope agreed. It is not a
        guarantee about the future, a certification, or ongoing monitoring.
        That's not a hedge — it's what makes the conclusions worth standing
        behind.
      </p>
      <div class="callout callout--boundary">
        <span class="callout__label">Boundaries</span>
        <ul class="boundary-list">
          <li>Regulatory findings are technical observations, not legal advice. Where interpretation needs a lawyer, the report says so.</li>
          <li>This is an expert architecture and code review, not a CREST-accredited penetration test. When one is needed, I refer a CREST partner.</li>
          <li>Every statement of work carries an itemised scope and a limitation of liability — you'll see both before signing.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Next step</span>
      <h2>Ready when you are</h2>
      <p>
        Pick the review that fits, or describe your situation and I'll tell you
        which one does.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/services/" class="btn btn--on-dark">See the three audits</a>
        <a href="/contact/" class="dark-link">or start a conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .process {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }
  .process__step {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .process__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .process__head h2 { margin: 0; }
  .process__num { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .boundary-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1em; }
  .boundary-list li { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .callout { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .dark-link { color: var(--gray-400); }
  .dark-link:hover { color: var(--gray-50); }
</style>
